te stones were thin, and Black stayed in the lower-left instead."}, {"turn": 31, "text": "A2 lost another 7.8 points, taking the score from -5.5 to -13.3. By then Black had already been behind by 9 or more points since move 23, and the engine still preferred E7."}, {"turn": 32, "text": "The 14k answered with D7, which lost 9.3 points and brought the lead back from -13.3 to -4.0. It was the 14k's worst move of the game, and the engine's choice was B4. Opus 5.5 took B4 on the next turn, losing 0.0 points, but the gap was still too large to close."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py flood-fills groups on a pasted board to print stones and liberty counts with a danger flag, and count.py flood-fills empty regions to tally area score and dead-stone-adjusted territory. Both only analyze the current position as given and never generate, score, or rank candidate moves or look ahead.", "stop": false}}